From 476f8236292f1e5e2069601b29812ae9f5b0187f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Wed, 8 Apr 2026 08:43:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] App: drop penaltyFlashScreen to avoid system_server watchdog
 kill loop

on debug builds (userdebug or eng) Seedvault registers a thread
StrictMode policy with penaltyFlashScreen(). on GSI builds running
on vendor HWC blobs with known BLAST queue creation issues (e.g.
mediatek mtk_common on MT6789), showing the red flash constructs
a BLASTBufferQueue which hangs indefinitely in nativeCreate,
system_server is blocked in WindowManagerService.showStrictModeViolation
for 60 seconds, the watchdog kills it, system_server respawns,
Seedvault is restarted as a backup transport service, its strictmode
policy re-initializes, another disk read on startup triggers another
flash request, and the whole cycle starts over.

keep detectAll + penaltyLog so the violations are still logged, but
never ask WindowManager to draw the flash.
---
 app/src/main/java/com/stevesoltys/seedvault/App.kt | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/stevesoltys/seedvault/App.kt b/app/src/main/java/com/stevesoltys/seedvault/App.kt
index 5c9a4cd..b13e1a5 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/com/stevesoltys/seedvault/App.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/com/stevesoltys/seedvault/App.kt
@@ -116,12 +116,15 @@ open class App : Application() {
             migrateToOwnScheduling()
             migrateToUnifiedScheduling()
         }
+        // penaltyFlashScreen() disabled: on GSI builds running on vendor HWC blobs with
+        // known BLAST queue creation issues, showing the red flash triggers a system_server
+        // watchdog kill and an endless respawn loop. we keep detectAll + penaltyLog so the
+        // violations are still logged, but we never ask WindowManager to draw the flash.
         if (isDebugBuild()) {
             StrictMode.setThreadPolicy(
                 StrictMode.ThreadPolicy.Builder()
                     .detectAll()
                     .penaltyLog()
-                    .penaltyFlashScreen()
                     .build()
             )
             StrictMode.setVmPolicy(
